  "core": {
    "name": "Reclaim The World Core",
    "short": "The required base for the Reclaim The World mods for Infection Free Zone. It reads the game for them and gives their windows the game's own look. Does nothing visible on its own: install it, then add Settlement Panel and/or Supply Lines.",
    "html": "<h3>Description</h3>\n<p><strong>Reclaim The World</strong> is a set of mods built around one idea: settlements left behind keep working. When the convoy moves on, the old settlement's surplus keeps arriving, like supply lines. Reclaim the map region by region.</p>\n<p><strong>Reclaim The World Core</strong> is the shared base under all of them. It reads the running game once and hands the numbers to the modules, gives their windows the same look as the game's own panels, and offers a small public API so anyone can build a module on top. Core only reads the game; it never changes anything. Core alone shows nothing in game.</p>\n<p>The modules (each has its own Nexus page, each needs Core):</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Reclaim The World Settlement Panel</strong>: an in-game panel (F8) with the settlement's production and resource balance.</li><li><strong>Reclaim The World Supply Lines</strong>: the settlement left behind keeps producing; its surplus arrives in the new settlement's stock at sunrise.</li></ul>\n<h4>For modders</h4>\n<p>Core is open source under the MIT licence. Anyone can build a module on it: a separate DLL and window, the same game data and the same look. The developer kit is available on request: a line on the Nexus Posts tab or in the <a href=\"https://github.com/Dimi-GE/ifz-reclaim-the-world/issues\">GitHub issues</a> is enough. No promise of more than that for now.</p>\n<p>Unofficial fan mod. Not affiliated with the developers of Infection Free Zone. Contains no game files or game code.</p>\n<h3>Installation</h3>\n<p>Needs BepInEx 5 (a mod loader) once. Then Core.</p>\n<ol><li>Find the game folder: in Steam, right-click Infection Free Zone, then Manage, then Browse local files. The folder with <code>Infection Free Zone.exe</code> is the game folder.</li><li>Install BepInEx: download <code>BepInEx_win_x64_5.4.23.x.zip</code> (the newest 5.4.23 version) from the <a href=\"https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases\">BepInEx releases page</a> and unzip it into the game folder. A <code>BepInEx</code> folder and a <code>winhttp.dll</code> now sit next to the exe. Start the game once and quit at the main menu so BepInEx creates its folders.</li><li>Install Core: download <code>ReclaimTheWorld.Core.zip</code> and extract it into <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\</code>. Result: <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\ReclaimTheWorld\\ReclaimTheWorld.Core.dll</code>.</li></ol>\n<p>Extract the zip (right-click, Extract All), don't copy the folder out of it. Every Reclaim The World zip holds a folder named <code>ReclaimTheWorld</code>, so copying the next one asks to replace the previous. BepInEx finds the DLLs in any folder under <code>plugins\\</code>.</p>\n<p>Then add the modules from their pages.</p>\n<h4>Updating</h4>\n<p>Close the game, replace the files in <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code> with the new ones. After a Core update, check that the modules are new enough (see their pages).</p>\n<h4>Uninstalling</h4>\n<p>Delete <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code> and <code>BepInEx\\config\\dge.rtw.core.cfg</code>. The modules stop working without Core. After file output or Supply Lines, also delete <code>BepInEx\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code> (this removes the old-settlement data).</p>\n<h4>Something's wrong?</h4>\n<ul><li>Nothing happens: check that <code>BepInEx\\LogOutput.log</code> exists. If not, BepInEx isn't loading; re-check step 2.</li><li>A module doesn't load: the log says it needs Core. Install or update Core.</li><li>After a game update mods can break; check for a new version.</li></ul>\n<p>Report problems on the Nexus Bugs tab or in the <a href=\"https://github.com/Dimi-GE/ifz-reclaim-the-world/issues\">GitHub issues</a> with <code>BepInEx\\LogOutput.log</code> and the game version (shown in the main menu).</p>\n<h3>Main features</h3>\n<ul><li>Reads the running game once and shares the data with every module.</li><li>A style kit: windows that look like the game's own panels (fonts, colours, frame, tiles, icons).</li><li>A small public API for module authors (open source, MIT).</li><li>Read-only: never changes the game.</li><li>Cleans up its own per-save files when a save is deleted.</li><li>Optional debug output: <code>WriteFile = true</code> in <code>BepInEx\\config\\dge.rtw.core.cfg</code> writes the data it reads to <code>BepInEx\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code>. Off by default.</li></ul>\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<p>Requires BepInEx 5.4.23.x (not BepInEx 6).</p>\n<p>Download: <a href=\"https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases\">BepInEx releases page</a></p>\n<p>Tested on Infection Free Zone 0.26.10.21 II BETA, BepInEx 5.4.23.5. Version 2.2.0.</p>\n<h3>Shout-outs</h3>\n<ul><li>The BepInEx team, for the mod loader that makes all of this possible.</li><li>JaySNL, for publishing modding notes that were the first way into the game.</li></ul>"
  },
