    "html": "<h3>Description</h3>\n<p><strong>Reclaim The World Settlement Panel</strong> shows the settlement's economy in one window, drawn inside the game in the game's own style. F8 shows what the buildings make and use, how each resource is doing, and who is working where, without clicking through building after building.</p>\n<p>It only reads the game; it never changes anything. With Reclaim The World Supply Lines it also pages through the old settlements.</p>\n<p>Part of the Reclaim The World mods: settlements left behind keep working.</p>\n<p>Unofficial fan mod. Not affiliated with the developers of Infection Free Zone. Contains no game files or game code.</p>\n<h3>Installation</h3>\n<p>Requires Reclaim The World Core 2.1.1 or newer: install <a href=\"core.html\">Reclaim The World Core</a> first (it also explains how to install BepInEx).</p>\n<ol><li>Download <code>ReclaimTheWorld.SettlementPanel.zip</code>.</li><li>Extract it into <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\</code> (right-click, Extract All). Don't copy the folder out of the zip: every Reclaim The World zip holds a folder with the same name, so copying replaces the other mods' folder.</li><li>Start the game, load a save and press <strong>F8</strong>. Change the key in <code>BepInEx\\config\\dge.rtw.settlementpanel.cfg</code>.</li></ol>\n<h4>Updating</h4>\n<p>Close the game, replace the DLL in <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code> with the new one.</p>\n<h4>Uninstalling</h4>\n<p>Delete <code>ReclaimTheWorld.SettlementPanel.dll</code> from <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code> and <code>BepInEx\\config\\dge.rtw.settlementpanel.cfg</code>.</p>\n<h4>Something's wrong?</h4>\n<p>If the panel doesn't load, <code>BepInEx\\LogOutput.log</code> says it needs Reclaim The World Core: install or update Core. Report problems on the Nexus Bugs tab or in the <a href=\"https://github.com/Dimi-GE/ifz-reclaim-the-world/issues\">GitHub issues</a> with <code>BepInEx\\LogOutput.log</code> and the game version (shown in the main menu).</p>\n<h3>Main features</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Header</strong>: working hours today, people, weather, temperature and mood. Details on hover.</li><li><strong>Resource grid</strong>: <strong>LOOP</strong> (what the production buildings use and make) or <strong>ALL</strong>. Click a resource to filter the lists below, click again for all.</li><li><strong>Production</strong>: one row per building type with count, workers and recipes.</li><li><strong>Balance</strong>: per resource, yesterday (<strong>DAY</strong>) or today so far (<strong>NOW</strong>): Produced, Supplies, Used, Net, Stock and Status. Supplies is what arrived from old settlements (Supply Lines).</li><li><strong>Settlement pager</strong> (with Supply Lines): arrows page through the old settlements and show what each one supplies.</li><li><strong>Footer</strong>: the installed Reclaim The World versions, handy for bug reports.</li><li>Styled like the game's own windows; stays out of the way of the map and closes with Esc.</li></ul>\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<p>Requires Reclaim The World Core 2.1.1 or newer. Get it here: <a href=\"core.html\">Reclaim The World Core</a>. Core needs BepInEx 5.4.23.x (not BepInEx 6).</p>\n<p>Tested on Infection Free Zone 0.26.10.21 II BETA, BepInEx 5.4.23.5. Version 0.12.0.</p>\n<h3>Shout-outs</h3>\n<ul><li>The BepInEx team, for the mod loader that makes all of this possible.</li></ul>"
