    "html": "<h3>Description</h3>\n<p><strong>Reclaim The World Supply Lines</strong> makes migrating pay off: the settlement left behind keeps working, like a supply line.</p>\n<p>When the convoy moves on, the mod records the old settlement: what its buildings with workers made yesterday, minus what they used and what the people left behind still eat. That is its line. At every sunrise in the new settlement, the surplus of each resource lands in its stock and the shortfalls are taken from it. Scavenging stops when the convoy leaves, so it isn't counted. Move again and the earlier settlements keep supplying: old settlements chain.</p>\n<p><strong>This mod changes the stock</strong> once a day at sunrise, adding and removing resources. These changes end up in the saves like any game change. Install it <strong>before migrating</strong>: the settlement is recorded at the moment the convoy leaves.</p>\n<p>If a shipment doesn't fit in the stock, the rest is carried over and arrives at the next sunrise. A shortfall is taken only as far as the stock goes and is never carried over. An old settlement's own leftover stock covers its own shortfalls first.</p>\n<p>Works best with Reclaim The World Settlement Panel, which pages through the old settlements and shows what each one supplies. Part of the Reclaim The World mods.</p>\n<p>Unofficial fan mod. Not affiliated with the developers of Infection Free Zone. Contains no game files or game code.</p>\n<h3>Installation</h3>\n<p>Requires Reclaim The World Core 2.2.0 or newer: install <a href=\"core.html\">Reclaim The World Core</a> first (it also explains how to install BepInEx).</p>\n<ol><li>Download <code>ReclaimTheWorld.SupplyLines.zip</code>.</li><li>Extract it into <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\</code> (right-click, Extract All). Don't copy the folder out of the zip: every Reclaim The World zip holds a folder with the same name, so copying replaces the other mods' folder.</li><li>Install it <strong>before migrating</strong>. Then play as usual.</li></ol>\n<p>Old-settlement data lives in <code>BepInEx\\ReclaimTheWorld\\SupplyLines\\</code>. Delete it and the old settlements are gone.</p>\n<p>Want to see what it would do without changing anything? Set <code>WriteStock = false</code> in <code>BepInEx\\config\\dge.rtw.supplylines.cfg</code>: it only logs what would happen. Its log lines in <code>BepInEx\\LogOutput.log</code> start with <code>sunrise day</code>.</p>\n<h4>Updating</h4>\n<p>Close the game, replace the DLL in <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code> with the new one.</p>\n<h4>Uninstalling</h4>\n<p>Delete <code>ReclaimTheWorld.SupplyLines.dll</code> from <code>BepInEx\\plugins\\ReclaimTheWorld\\</code> and <code>BepInEx\\config\\dge.rtw.supplylines.cfg</code>. Old settlements stop supplying; stock changes already made stay in the saves. To remove the old-settlement data too, delete <code>BepInEx\\ReclaimTheWorld\\SupplyLines\\</code>.</p>\n<h4>Something's wrong?</h4>\n<p>If it doesn't load, <code>BepInEx\\LogOutput.log</code> says it needs Reclaim The World Core: install or update Core. Report problems on the Nexus Bugs tab or in the <a href=\"https://github.com/Dimi-GE/ifz-reclaim-the-world/issues\">GitHub issues</a> with <code>BepInEx\\LogOutput.log</code> and the game version (shown in the main menu).</p>\n<h3>Main features</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Departure record</strong>: when the convoy leaves, the settlement is saved with what it made, used and eats.</li><li><strong>Claim on arrival</strong>: at the first save of the new settlement, the mod finds the settlement the convoy came from.</li><li><strong>Sunrise shipments and penalties</strong>: surplus is added to the stock, shortfalls are taken from it, netted across all old settlements.</li><li><strong>Overflow carried over</strong>: what doesn't fit arrives at the next sunrise.</li><li><strong>Chain</strong>: migrate again and the earlier settlements keep supplying.</li><li><strong>Safe switch</strong>: <code>WriteStock = false</code> logs only, changes nothing.</li><li><strong>Log lines</strong> starting with <code>sunrise day</code> show every shipment and penalty.</li><li><strong>Pager</strong> in Reclaim The World Settlement Panel: page through old settlements, and the Balance list shows a Supplies column.</li></ul>\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<p>Requires Reclaim The World Core 2.2.0 or newer. Get it here: <a href=\"core.html\">Reclaim The World Core</a>. Core needs BepInEx 5.4.23.x (not BepInEx 6). Reclaim The World Settlement Panel is recommended to see the old settlements.</p>\n<p>Tested on Infection Free Zone 0.26.10.21 II BETA, BepInEx 5.4.23.5. Version 0.5.0.</p>\n<h3>Shout-outs</h3>\n<ul><li>The BepInEx team, for the mod loader that makes all of this possible.</li></ul>"
